WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:02.130
So the artists' books--
artists' books in general,

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.450
they're kind of hard to define.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.500
But here at MIT, what
we've defined them

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.610
as for the sake
of our collection

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:11.370
is a contemporary form
of art in which artists,

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:15.330
or a group of artists, take
the codex, or book form,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.510
and just play with it
however they'd like.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.750
And that can be in form,
structure, or content.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.660
Artists' books can provide
another way in to material--

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.260
can provide another way
to engage with dialogue,

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.280
or with historical events, or
with scientific discoveries--

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.280
in a visual and
tactile way that can

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.960
be lacking in the classroom.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.940
I'm looking to
collaborate with faculty,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.644
and bringing them
into the classroom,

00:00:40.644 --> 00:00:42.810
and getting students to
really just experience them.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.030
Because you know, I can talk
about them all day long.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.630
But if you don't see them,
if you don't touch them,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.550
if you don't play
with them yourself,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.580
then I could just talk, and
it wouldn't mean anything.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.040
Because you see all the
work that the artists have

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.010
put into it, and all of the
care, and all of the thought,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.940
and it's really just so
detailed that it's amazing.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.580
It's indescribable.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.940
These books are pieces
of art, but also

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.450
really influential pieces
in the dialogue of society.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:14.650
And the potential for
them is unlimited.

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.650
So students can create
their own artists' books.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.200
They can make their own
works based on whatever

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.370
matters to them right now.

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:23.850
Really, the possibilities
are endless.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.200
[MUSIC PLAYING]

